# The three "is the loop / the poller alive" alerts, lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml
# (comments stripped — the manifest is their one home) — the rules file that
# loop-health.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test
# rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under
# `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on
# purpose — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest
# there would fail it.
#
# This is the SECOND fixture over github-exporter's rule file (queued-age.promtool-* was the
# first, FU-150/#284) and it covers 3 of the file's 13 alerts. The other 9 have no behaviour test
# yet — homelab#288 shipped the two spend/agent-loop files the issue named first and this much of
# the third; the rest is honest remaining work, listed in that PR's body.
#
# ⚠ NOT DRIFT-PINNED (unlike queued-age.promtool-rules, which `devbox run exporter-self-test`
# checks): the general harness that would extract `.spec.groups` at run time lives in `scripts/**`
# + `.github/**`, outside the fixer lane's tier. Re-copy after editing an alert:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups": [{"name": "github", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] |
#        select(.alert == "AgentQueueStalled" or .alert == "GithubExporterDown" or
#               .alert == "GithubExporterStale")]}]}' \
#     argocd/resources/github-exporter/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
#
# …that command regenerates the `github` group ONLY. The `regression-witness-pre-313` group at the
# bottom is not in the CR and must survive the re-copy — re-append it (see its own header).
groups:
  - name: github
    rules:
      - alert: GithubExporterDown
        expr: up{job="github-exporter"} == 0
        for: 15m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: github-exporter is not being scraped
          description: The GitHub poller pod is down or unreachable for 15m — no CI-failure or billing alerts until it's back. Usually the token Secret is missing (ExternalSecret github-exporter-token) or the pod crashed.
      - alert: GithubExporterStale
        expr: time() - max by (job) (max_over_time(github_exporter_last_success_timestamp[10m])) > 1800
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: github-exporter polls are failing
          description: 'No fully successful GitHub poll for 30m+ — likely the PAT expired/was revoked. Re-mint: scripts/github-exporter-pat-bootstrap.sh (docs/github-setup.md §Tokens).'
      - alert: AgentQueueStalled
        expr: sum(github_agent_issue_labels{label="agent/queued"}) > 0 and (sum(kube_pod_status_phase{phase=~"Running|Pending", pod=~"agent-.+-(issue|pr)-[0-9]+-r[0-9]+|agent-.+-[0-9]{6}"}) or vector(0)) == 0 and (sum(github_pull_request_open) or vector(0)) == 0
        for: 2h
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: Agent queue stalled — queued issues but a fully idle loop
          description: '{{ $value }} agent/queued issue(s) with zero live workers and zero open PRs for 2h — check the coordinate ticks (kubectl -n oracle-agents get wf), the WIP holds in the scan report, and agents/coordinator/TICK-LOG.md for the last incident shape.'

  # ── REGRESSION WITNESS — NOT a deployed rule, and deliberately not in prometheusrule.yaml ─────
  # The pre-#313 GithubExporterStale expr, kept verbatim so the fixture can assert the FAILURE it
  # fixes instead of merely asserting the fix. The roll cases in loop-health.promtool-test check
  # both alerts at the same eval times: this one goes silent across the roll and re-pages 12m late
  # under the new pod's identity, the shipped one never notices. Same device #288 used
  # (openrouter-proxy/subscription.promtool-rules §regression-witness-pre-288), and for the same
  # reason: it makes the contrast executed rather than claimed.
  # If GithubExporterStale's expr is revisited, this stays as it is — it is a fossil of what must
  # not come back, not a copy of the live rule. It is also why a STALE hand copy of the group above
  # cannot pass vacuously: with the old expr in both places the two alerts would agree, and every
  # roll assertion below fails.
  - name: regression-witness-pre-313
    rules:
      - alert: GithubExporterStalePre313
        expr: time() - github_exporter_last_success_timestamp > 1800
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: github-exporter polls are failing
